rol_pair_din.py','control_separate_base.py'])]; ast.parse(pathlib.Path('candidate.py').read_text())\\\\\\\"\\\"},\n 'assessment_policy':{'selection':'validation macro_auc equal weight over all4 labels; ties macro_logloss, then parameters, then trial_id','required_reporting':'All task AUC/Logloss deltas versus baseline and both frozen sources; macro scores; parameters, train/wall/inference times and peak GPU memory; every failed/deferred receipt. Never average missing tasks.','slices':'Preserve existing predeclared empty,1-16,17-64,>64 history bins and counts. Empty buy has13 positives: descriptive only. Other requested slices require host availability/training-defined bins; do not invent absent diagnostics.','uncertainty':'Single seed preliminary; user-cluster paired bootstrap only if authorized predictions/user clusters and budget are available. Do not bootstrap impression rows as independent users.','test':'Unavailable and forbidden in this phase; no held-out requests. Freeze validation suite now.','utility_vs_mechanism':'Beating frozen g0 is utility evidence. Beating the DIN replacement is provisional controlled aggregation evidence. Neither establishes repeated support or external novelty.'},\n 'memory_handoff':{'write_scope':'No writable agent-memory endpoint/path is supplied in this proposal phase. Preserve evidence.jsonl and human-owned sources; submit these provenance-linked records for host append-only ingestion, without claiming ingestion already occurred.','records':[{'maturity':'local_observation','evidence_refs':['g0-r0017-pair_rank_occupancy','g1-r0009-compact_mean'],'observation':'Source AST inspection shows compact source omits pair banks and uses separate feedback memory; the stronger source uses pair banks and collapsed feedback. Hence raw source-score difference cannot isolate aggregation.'},{'maturity':'hypothesis','evidence_refs':['g0-r0017-pair_rank_occupancy','g1-r0009-compact_mean'],'observation':'A compact valid-event mean residual may complement pair occupancy; proposed factorial and active DIN replacement have no measured outcomes yet.'}]},\n 'trajectory_review':{'available':['baseline-din','g0-r0017-pair_rank_occupancy','g1-r0009-compact_mean'],'unavailable':'Task summary mentions unsuccessful hybrid/blend branches, but scoped agent search hybrid blend compact returned no records. No scores or causal conclusions are fabricated; prior failure details remain unavailable.','new_results':'None. Proposed variants are not measured improvements.'},\n 'reproduction':'Host consumes each standalone module and its exact variants[].config under protocol '+protocol+' using its authorized scratch-training interface. No training CLI is supplied in this phase; do not invent one. Reuse a historical cell only if source/protocol/data hashes and host parity checks agree.'\n}\nPath('proposal.json').write_text(json.dumps(proposal,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nprint('Wrote proposal.json with3 variants,3 contrasts,2x2 source/residual cells, measured source table and provenance.')\ntry:\n import jsonschema\n jsonschema.validate(proposal['study'],r['study_schema'])\n print('Study JSON Schema validation passed.')\nexcept ImportError:\n print('jsonschema unavailable: checking strict study fields/types manually.')\n schema=r['study_schema']\n assert set(proposal['study'])==set(schema['required'])\n for k,s in schema['properties'].items():\n  assert isinstance(proposal['study'][k],{'string':str,'array':list,'object':dict}[s['type']]),k\n for n in proposal['study']['nearest_work']:\n  assert set(n)=={'source_ref','verification','difference'}\n for n in proposal['study']['contrasts']:\n  assert set(n)==set(schema['properties']['contrasts']['items']['required'])\n assert set(proposal['study']['cost_plan'])==set(schema['properties']['cost_plan']['required'])\n print('Strict study structure/types and nested required fields passed.')\nfor v in variants:\n assert Path(v['file']).name==v['file'] and v['file'].endswith('.py')\n assert v['config']==config(v['file'])\nprint('Variant standalone paths and literal configs match.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
